**Cache usage patterns**:

```
Session Cache (Redis DB 0):
├── TTL: User session duration (default 24h)
├── Pattern: user:session:{token} → User object
├── Eviction: TTL-based
└── Size: ~500MB

API Response Cache (Redis DB 1):
├── TTL: 5 minutes - 1 hour based on endpoint
├── Pattern: api:cache:{endpoint}:{params_hash} → Response
├── Eviction: LRU + TTL
└── Size: ~5GB

Rate Limiting (Redis DB 2):
├── TTL: 1 minute (sliding window)
├── Pattern: ratelimit:{partner_id}:{endpoint} → Token count
├── Eviction: TTL-based
└── Size: ~100MB

Profile State Cache (Redis DB 3):
├── TTL: 5 minutes
├── Pattern: profile:state:{iccid} → State enum
├── Eviction: TTL + write-through invalidation
└── Size: ~2GB

Catalog Cache (Redis DB 4):
├── TTL: 1 hour
├── Pattern: plan:catalog:{country} → Plan list
├── Eviction: Manual invalidation on plan updates
└── Size: ~500MB

Distributed Locks (Redis DB 5):
├── TTL: Operation timeout (30s - 5min)
├── Pattern: lock:{resource}:{id} → Lock owner
├── Eviction: TTL-based
└── Size: ~50MB
```

